apt-snapshot-guard (1.0.28) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Cancel a timed-out snapshot on both paths, not just the socket one. Since the CLI cutover both branches run the same Go client, which only watches a job the daemon owns -- so killing it on a timeout stopped nothing, and apt was refused while rsync kept writing and holding the repository write lock. TS_CLIENT now defaults to /usr/bin/timeshift.

