apt-snapshot-guard (1.0.27) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Removing this package no longer breaks apt. The apt hook file survived
    removal while the script it called did not, so every later apt command
    failed -- including the reinstall that would have fixed it
  * A snapshot no longer fails just because the Timeshift service is busy or
    was upgraded without being restarted; it falls back to the command line
  * A snapshot that times out is cancelled rather than left running
  * A bypass flag that cannot be removed no longer disables the guard silently
    and permanently
  * A misspelt ENABLED value keeps the guard on instead of switching it off
  * The graphical prompt can no longer hold apt open indefinitely
  * The timeout is now the total time apt can be delayed, not double it

