apt-snapshot-guard (1.0.16) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Backup/restore: transfer extended attributes (-X). rsync's archive mode omits them, so every security.capability was silently dropped - a restored snap-confine lost its ten file capabilities and broke every snap on the system, and ping/mtr-packet lost cap_net_raw
  * Restore: warn when the restored snap-confine has no file capabilities, which is what any snapshot taken before -X produces

