apt-snapshot-guard (1.0.15) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Backup/restore: keep /snap/bin and /snap/<name>/current - excluding all of /snap also dropped the symlinks every snap command resolves through, so a restored system had all its .snap payloads and still reported the snap was not installed
  * Restore: warn when the target has snap payloads but no /snap/bin, which is what restoring a snapshot taken before this change produces

