apt-snapshot-guard (1.0.12) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Restore: the reconnect probe no longer shares the ssh ControlMaster socket - a client attaching to a wedged master never performs connect(2), so ConnectTimeout did not apply and the probe blocked instead of dialling afresh
  * Restore: drop the shared ssh connection before each reconnect attempt, and remove stale control sockets that rmdir could never reap
  * Restore: reconnect banner now shows the attempt, elapsed time and what the drop was, and states that re-running resumes
  * Add a Retry action when a remote snapshot location is unavailable, instead of only offering to reconfigure it
  * Fix the capability cache being invalidated after the probe that filled it, which pinned a wrong reason for the whole session

 -- makeafide <willsmit4433@gmail.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:37:19 -0400

apt-snapshot-guard (1.0.11) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Restore: require an EFI System Partition when the snapshot came from a UEFI system - it was defaulting to 'keep on root', so the ESP was never mounted, the snapshot's EFI payload landed on ext4 and grub-install failed with 'cannot find EFI directory'
  * Restore: never use an ESP on a different disk from the root device - both front ends defaulted to the ESP of the machine running the restore, which would overwrite the live system's boot loader
  * Restore: show the snapshot's original layout against the target selection, and block on a missing / or /boot/efi
  * Restore: capture each post-restore step's output to /var/log/timeshift/restore-steps.log on the restored system

 -- makeafide <willsmit4433@gmail.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 15:53:19 -0400

apt-snapshot-guard (1.0.10) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Restore: fold mount points that duplicate an ancestor's device, and abort if an aliased mount reaches the transfer (this erased a restore target through <target>/home)
  * Restore: run the hardened sync script on the restore-to-another-device path, which previously discarded it along with the retry loop and the fail-closed sentinel
