apt-snapshot-guard (1.0.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Graphical bypass: when the snapshot fails during an interactive GUI update
    (Software Updater / GNOME Software via aptdaemon, or PackageKit) there is
    no terminal to prompt on, so a zenity dialog is now shown to the desktop
    user (Continue anyway / Cancel update). Runs de-escalated as the logged-in
    user, reconstructing the Wayland/X11 + D-Bus session env via loginctl.
  * Scope limited to aptdaemon/PackageKit; unattended-upgrades never prompts
    and still aborts on failure. New helper /usr/lib/apt-snapshot-guard/gui-prompt.
  * Config: GUI_PROMPT (default 1) and GUI_PROMPT_TIMEOUT (default 120s, 0 =
    wait). Recommends: zenity.

 -- makeafide <willsmit4433@gmail.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:20:00 -0400

apt-snapshot-guard (1.0.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Policy is now fail-CLOSED: apt does not change packages unless the
    snapshot succeeds, a bypass flag is set, or the user answers a prompt.
  * On snapshot failure at a terminal, prompt "Continue WITHOUT a restore
    point? [y/N]"; default No; PROMPT_TIMEOUT (default 60s) with no answer
    aborts. With no terminal (GUI updater, PackageKit, unattended-upgrades)
    the operation is aborted.
  * New one-shot bypass flag /run/apt-snapshot-guard.bypass: skip the
    snapshot for a single run; the flag is consumed (removed) when used.
  * Config: removed STRICT (always fail-closed now); added PROMPT_TIMEOUT.
    Helper now runs under bash (needs read -t).

